Fillets: a rounding's end cut by the faces at the end continued past
their bounds on the side of its second contact (mitcad#236).

A wall's foot rounded along the floor up to where a hole in the floor
beside the wall begins (the hole's side and a 45 degree chamfer of its
corner at the wall): the floor's contact meets the hole's side, while the
wall's contact runs on along the wall. The bodies stored in the .f3d files
cut the blend with the hole's side and chamfer continued up through it,
the wall's contact ending where the chamfer's plane meets it. In
PerformIntersectionAtEnd the end of the second contact (OnSame on the
stripe's second face) was sought on the last face's bounded surface
(fillets; chamfers since 0143 take it unbounded), so no point was found
("pb intersection Face - Fi").

- For fillets the end is now sought on that face's unbounded surface
  where the bounded one gives none (the point lies on the prolongation of
  the face's edge at the vertex).

Upstream: new.
